    {
      "id": "claim_e3f4d1c721774f69bd8ea8d5331b01f6",
      "statement": "The approval timeout is derived from the local MCP HTTP request timeout minus a buffer so Brijio returns a structured approval error before a generic HTTP timeout: approvalTimeoutMs = httpTimeoutMs - approvalTimeoutBufferMs, defaulting to 60000 - 5000 = 55000 ms. For deployments behind infrastructure Brijio does not control, it must be configured below the shortest upstream timeout.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L162-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce3359666f2787ed39a340a303ec34f8d54afcf6d9ef431d3dcebed8363ffc31:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/src/http-server.ts#L62-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b68f91d1467dac78e37bd2b08610ceb7f73449055f84d1b594e4495c6eb8811:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2bfb1bc9313e491aab2c1b47952e28ed",
      "statement": "Approval failures return structured error codes: approval_denied (user denied), approval_timeout (no response before the computed timeout), approval_unavailable (extension could not render the UI, e.g. missing actionUUID, no approval adapter, no active-tab origin, or banner injection failed), and approval_origin_changed (active origin changed before execution). Errors include actionUUID when available; batch errors follow existing aborted conventions.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0048-client-side-action-approval.md#L357-L367",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e25e3e6b57177a7aac2e4eb9f1dcec8259f14e4684c8f685f3a633fdfc83642f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/background-controller.ts#L1342-L1426",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e6593298f0a269a65878bdefe0a25768fde5e18b2ba5dfdccafb0aec373d0c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6be55607835848afb5fb35ef17a3e501",
      "statement": "The MCP server assigns a unique actionUUID to every approval-gated request and to every batch action, marking submit_form, fetch_resource, and download_file with approvalRequest: true. ApprovalMetadata (actionUUID and approvalRequest) is carried by every Perform*Action payload and by DownloadFileRequest/FetchResourceRequest in the shared protocol.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/protocol.ts#L420-L466",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac922ab271e920720995f2d72507c297877df64ac60e76d4a46693a50ab8b534:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://servers/mcp/src/websocket-client.ts#L860-L891",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:13eaa255f58ff8ccf2e35e91c579af0f470ee9933573a8865200947563d3df0b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8e617e63eacb4793bf2b1b76ac73b554",
      "statement": "Brijio's explicit non-goals, marked intentionally unsupported in the capability matrix, are: cookie export, session cloning, browser mirroring, continuous screenshots, continuous DOM streaming, background surveillance, browser history collection, credential extraction, and MFA interception. These are deliberate product boundaries, not missing features; password fields return browser_error on fill attempts.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/project/CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md#L165-L180",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:639774d8c3663b60623462b4739368c9351299ec9e7cbe029c04518a56ecc26e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/SECURITY_GUARANTEES.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:3626a37f667d817cce96ac5aba03bb25c6183302efe00e7bd3aadc3e93b32472"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9860eac1117446cbc6940dbe6bbe29e",
      "statement": "The threat model plans around four attacker classes: malicious agent, compromised relay server, network attacker, and malicious website. Mitigations are architectural rather than purely defensive code: explicit request/response protocol, no continuous streaming, user-controlled browser connection, progressive disclosure, TLS and auth tokens, relay-as-transport, and read-only structured page extraction that is never executed or evaluated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/THREAT_MODEL.md#L15-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:516eaac0b5bd356695be1732f5b0f14fe10cf05445fbbb54efc7f264e340498f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b5002d7ad2fd4f178b56aae90e11e5fc",
      "statement": "Trust is partitioned across four boundaries (Agent↔MCP, MCP↔relay, relay↔extension, extension↔session). The relay and extension authenticate with a pairing token and the MCP server with a separate MCP auth token; the relay routes messages without needing to inspect payloads, and the extension reads structured DOM without trusting or executing page content. Trust is explicitly not assumed for the network, cloud relay privacy, agent intent, or website content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/TRUST_BOUNDARIES.md#L9-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:99ce717fabcfbbcc610e3c7151a9f7fa3367a6298129217642436577f55faeab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/protocol.ts#L44-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf54b5232d0234743d279f57e4f9f664014f21329b735dd5aefde7131dde1673:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1c9cb31f44864e1393f1d4ff11f2ed22",
      "statement": "AGENTS.md defines non-negotiable invariants: the user explicitly starts/stops the bridge; browser state is available only while the user-controlled extension is connected; every read or action is an explicit MCP request with no continuous page/DOM/screenshot/history streaming; no silent surveillance, cookie export, credential extraction, session cloning, or MFA interception; and user-visible connection state and client-side action approval must be preserved without bypassing approval checks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L38-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:04ca3080466731e8f9b61dfb7de334f59f0e1af72138e5e9c570f2c25a692657:"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
